.TH SHB-RESTORE 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.4.0-prod" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb-restore \- Restore swapped secret files to their original real values
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb restore [path] [--all] [--orphans]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restores project secret files (.env) from the secure vault backup back to their original disk locations. Safely performs 3-way reconciliation so that newly added configuration keys and edited variables are preserved while real secrets are restored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-a\fR, \fB--all\fR
Restore swapped secret files across all registered projects
.TP
\fB-o\fR, \fB--orphans\fR
Restore orphaned swaps left by crashed or terminated processes
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
$ \fBshb restore\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb restore --all\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb restore --orphans\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb restore /path/to/project\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
shb(1)
.SH WEBSITE
https://secretharbor.dev
